WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:11.940
When a person considers and analyzes the functions
of the brain, the brain is analyzing itself.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:17.630
As far as the human brain is concerned, it
is the only thing on planet earth to have

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.350
the ability to become self-aware of its own
existence.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:29.920
Not only is the brain aware of its existence,
but it also spends its entire life trying

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.860
to understand why.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.110
Existing is not enough for the brain.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:38.950
The brain must also understand why.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:44.960
It is the single question “why?” that
separates human from all other species on

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.010
planet earth.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:53.690
Ever since we are old enough to utter words,
it seems as though our favorite word is, “why?”

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:59.030
When we are a child, we ask things like why
the sky is blue or why things die.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:05.900
Our parents might give us their best answers,
but the spirit of our question remains restless

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.040
and fundamentally unanswered.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.039
Our brain is so confused.

00:01:11.039 --> 00:01:18.240
It does not understand how it can be both
conscious enough to ask questions but not

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.259
conscious enough to uncover all of the answers?

00:01:23.259 --> 00:01:30.039
It taunts itself with this perpetual cycle,
trying to find a way out of its infinite madness,

00:01:30.039 --> 00:01:35.549
but it only knows how to digs its self deeper.

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:37.250
So what do we do?

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:41.429
Do we follow our brain into its hole of madness?

00:01:41.429 --> 00:01:43.289
Yes and no.

00:01:43.289 --> 00:01:49.590
We must be careful when we live with the word,
“why?” because it is a double-edged sword.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:57.850
On one side, it is a wasted existence to disregard
our inquisitive nature and not try to improve

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.829
life and human understanding.

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:06.999
But on the other side, identifying with this
infinite inquest fills us with a sense of

00:02:06.999 --> 00:02:14.349
constant dissatisfaction and restrains us
from ever truly stopping and enjoying our

00:02:14.349 --> 00:02:16.930
individual lives.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:22.420
It is a balance between both sides that we
must learn and apply.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.319
We must ask “why?”

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:31.180
but learn how to live happily without always
having an answer for it.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:35.280
If our well-being is dependent on all the
“whys?”

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.510
being answered, we become like a dog chasing
its own tail.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:46.489
We will constantly chase our brain, running
in circles, longing for all the answers to

00:02:46.489 --> 00:02:49.019
life.

00:02:49.019 --> 00:02:56.040
But once a dog catches its tail, it realizes
that the tail was a part of it the whole time

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.450
and it has only bitten itself.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:05.829
In the same way, people who try to find the
experience of life by merely chasing after

00:03:05.829 --> 00:03:08.129
it, suffer.

00:03:08.129 --> 00:03:14.170
Just like the tail is attached to the dog,
life is already attached to us.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.840
We do not always need to chase it.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:30.699
Sometimes we just need to live it and enjoy
its mystery.

